1
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
In love, there are no boundaries.

2
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
The English Patient is a drama, romance, war film directed by Anthony Minghella.

3
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:21,000
In the 1930s, Count Almásy is a Hungarian map maker employed by the Royal Geographical Society to chart
the vast expanses of the Sahara Desert along with several other prominent explorers.

4
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
As World War II unfolds, Almásy enters into a world
of love, betrayal, and politics.

5
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Almásy, played by Ralph Fiennes.

6
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Hana, played by Juliette Binoche.

7
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
David Caravaggio, played by Willem Dafoe.

8
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Katharine Clifton, played by Kristin Scott Thomas.

9
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:51,000
Sikh Kip, played by Naveen Andrews.

10
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Geoffrey Clifton, played by Colin Firth.

11
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
The English Patient is a 1996 epic romantic war drama film directed by Anthony Minghella from his
own script based on the 1992 novel by Michael Ondaatje, and produced by Saul Zaentz.

12
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film stars Ralph Fiennes and Kristin Scott Thomas alongside Juliette Binoche,
Willem Dafoe, Naveen Andrews and Colin Firth in supporting roles.

13
01:27:45,000 --> 01:27:51,000
The protagonist of the title, a man burned beyond recognition who speaks with an English accent, recalls his history in a series of
flashbacks, revealing to the audience his true identity and the love affair in which he was involved before the war.

14
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
The film ends with an onscreen statement that it is a fictionalized account of
László Almásy (died 1951) and other historical figures and events.

15
01:41:15,000 --> 01:41:21,000
The film received widespread critical acclaim and emerged as a
major commercial success at the box-office.

16
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
The film received twelve nominations at the 69th Academy Awards, winning nine, including Best
Picture, Best Director for Minghella, and Best Supporting Actress for Binoche.

17
01:54:45,000 --> 01:54:51,000
It was also the first to receive a Best Editing
Oscar for a digitally edited film.

18
02:01:30,000 --> 02:01:36,000
Ralph Fiennes, playing the titular character, and Kristin Scott
Thomas were Oscar-nominated for their performances.

19
02:08:15,000 --> 02:08:21,000
The film also won five BAFTA Awards and two Golden Globes.

20
02:15:00,000 --> 02:15:06,000
The British Film Institute ranked The English Patient the
55th-greatest British film of the 20th century.

21
02:21:45,000 --> 02:21:51,000
The American Film Institute ranked it the 56th-greatest love story of all time.

22
02:28:30,000 --> 02:28:36,000
The film explores themes of egypt, secret love, amnesia, airplane, cairo.

23
02:35:15,000 --> 02:35:21,000
The tone is emotional.
